// Seed part 1: core meanings (design section 6; built-ins.md section 3).
//
// The closed list everything bottoms out in. A reduction that needs a meaning outside this file
// (and outside the structural concepts of built-ins.md section 4) does not reduce. Each entry
// passes the test of built-ins.md section 1: it would be in the list for chess, a jam website and
// the user's name, and for a cooking assistant or a calendar.
//
// Sources of the list: Wierzbicka and Goddard's semantic primes, VerbNet 3.4's semantic
// predicates, and the document heads of design section 25b. Where a prime or predicate is already
// a structural concept (Not, If, Every, Some, Only, Before, After, Now, Kind, Quote, Speaker,
// Addressee) or a pure primitive (Contains, Compare, Count), it is not repeated here.
//
// Naming: a core meaning has the name its English exponent's word concept would have, and is that
// concept (seed/README.md, decision 1). Lemma facts record the exponent. Two-place states take
// their arguments positionally (Have(owner, thing)); events take roles.
//
// Frame(...) says what a core meaning takes and of what kind. Values are LF kinds (Prop, Act,
// Thing, Time, Kind) or core kinds (Someone, Something, Place, Amount).

Pack(name="seed-core", version="0.1.0", from=Seed("core"))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Roles (ncon.md section 7). The roles function words assign and core meanings take. VerbNet's
// thematic roles are imported and made SameAs these where they are the same.

Concept(Role())

Concept(Agent(), IsA(Role()))          // who or what does it
Concept(Patient(), IsA(Role()))        // what is changed by it
Concept(Theme(), IsA(Role()))          // what is moved, had, said or known, unchanged
Concept(Experiencer(), IsA(Role()))    // who knows, wants, feels or sees
Concept(Stimulus(), IsA(Role()))       // what is seen, heard or felt
Concept(Recipient(), IsA(Role()))      // who ends up having it
Concept(Beneficiary(), IsA(Role()))    // for whom it is done
Concept(Source(), IsA(Role()))         // where it starts or comes from
Concept(Destination(), IsA(Role()))    // where it ends up
Concept(Location(), IsA(Role()))       // where it is or happens
Concept(Path(), IsA(Role()))           // the way it goes
Concept(Spatial(), IsA(Role()))        // where, in space: a location or a path
Fact(Path(), IsA(Spatial()))
Fact(Location(), IsA(Spatial()))
Fact(Source(), IsA(Path()))            // where a path starts
Fact(Destination(), IsA(Path()))       // where a path ends
Concept(Instrument(), IsA(Role()))     // what it is done with
Concept(Topic(), IsA(Role()))          // what it is about
Concept(Attribute(), IsA(Role()))      // which property
Concept(Value(), IsA(Role()))          // what the property is
Concept(Extent(), IsA(Role()))         // how much or how far
Concept(Standard(), IsA(Role()))       // what it is compared with
Concept(Result(), IsA(Role()))         // what holds because of it
Concept(Purpose(), IsA(Role()))        // what it is done for
Concept(Reason(), IsA(Role()))         // why it happens
Concept(Material(), IsA(Role()))       // what a made thing is made from
Concept(Product(), IsA(Role()))        // what is made
Concept(Partner(), IsA(Role()))        // who or what it is done with
Concept(Content(), IsA(Role()))        // the words or block a document part holds
Concept(Level(), IsA(Role()))          // a heading's depth
Concept(Done(), IsA(Role()))           // whether a task is done
Concept(Language(), IsA(Role()))       // a code block's language
Concept(To(), IsA(Role()))             // a link's target
Concept(Alt(), IsA(Role()))            // an image's alternative text

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Substantives

Concept(Someone(), Lemma("someone"), IsA(Something()))
Concept(Something(), Lemma("something"))
Concept(People(), Lemma("people"), IsA(Someone()))
Concept(Part(), Lemma("part"), Frame(Thing()))                            // a part of a whole
Concept(PartOf(), Lemma("part of"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))              // X is part of Y
Concept(Place(), Lemma("place"), IsA(Something()))
Concept(Way(), Lemma("way"), Frame(Act()))                                // how something is done
Concept(Word(), Lemma("word"), IsA(Something()))
Concept(Name(), Lemma("name"), Frame(Thing()))                            // what something is called
Concept(Number(), Lemma("number"), IsA(Amount()))
Concept(Amount(), Lemma("amount"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(State(), Lemma("state"), Frame(Thing()))                          // how something is, at a time
Concept(Oneself(), Frame(Someone()))                                      // the same someone as the agent

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Determination and identity

Concept(This(), Lemma("this"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Same(), Lemma("same"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))
Concept(Other(), Lemma("other"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                 // not the same as
Concept(Like(), Lemma("like"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                   // similar to
Concept(Be(), Lemma("be"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                       // X is Y (identity or kind)
Concept(Exist(), Lemma("exist"), Lemma("there is"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Have(), Lemma("have"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                   // X has Y
Concept(BeIn(), Lemma("be in"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                  // X is in Y
Concept(Together(), Lemma("together"), Frame(Thing()))                    // the members are one
Concept(Touch(), Lemma("touch"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Quantity

Concept(One(), Lemma("one"), IsA(Number()))
Concept(Two(), Lemma("two"), IsA(Number()))
Concept(Many(), Lemma("many"), Lemma("much"), Frame(Kind()))
Concept(Few(), Lemma("few"), Lemma("little"), Frame(Kind()))
Concept(More(), Lemma("more"), Frame(Thing(), standard=Thing(), attribute=Kind()))
Concept(Less(), Lemma("less"), Frame(Thing(), standard=Thing(), attribute=Kind()))
Concept(Most(), Lemma("most"), Frame(Kind(), attribute=Kind()))
Concept(Enough(), Lemma("enough"), Frame(Thing(), purpose=Act()))
Concept(Excess(), Lemma("too"), Frame(Thing(), purpose=Act()))            // more than is good for
Concept(Very(), Lemma("very"), Frame(Prop()))
Concept(Also(), Lemma("also"), Frame(Prop()))                             // this as well as the other
Concept(Whole(), Lemma("whole"), Frame(Thing()))                          // every part of it
Concept(First(), Lemma("first"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                 // nothing before it in an order
Concept(Last(), Lemma("last"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                   // nothing after it in an order
Concept(Next(), Lemma("next"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                   // right after, in an order
Concept(Order(), Lemma("order"), Frame(Thing(), attribute=Kind()))        // members one after another

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Evaluation and description

Concept(Good(), Lemma("good"), Frame(Thing(), beneficiary=Someone()))
Concept(Bad(), Lemma("bad"), Frame(Thing(), beneficiary=Someone()))
Concept(True(), Lemma("true"), Frame(Prop()))
Concept(Big(), Lemma("big"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Small(), Lemma("small"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Long(), Lemma("long"), Frame(Thing()))                            // in length or in time
Concept(Short(), Lemma("short"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(New(), Lemma("new"), Frame(Thing()))                              // began to exist a short time before
Concept(Old(), Lemma("old"), Frame(Thing()))                              // began to exist a long time before
Concept(Open(), Lemma("open"), Frame(Thing()))                            // can be gone into, used or added to
Concept(Work(), Lemma("work"), Frame(Thing()))                            // does what it is for
Concept(Important(), Lemma("important"), Frame(Thing()))                  // do not miss this (also a document head)
Concept(Easy(), Lemma("easy"), Frame(Act(), beneficiary=Someone()))
Concept(Possible(), Lemma("possible"), Frame(Prop()))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Mind

Concept(Think(), Lemma("think"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), topic=Prop()))
Concept(Know(), Lemma("know"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), theme=Thing()))
Concept(Want(), Lemma("want"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), theme=Prop()))
Concept(Need(), Lemma("need"), Frame(experiencer=Thing(), theme=Thing()))    // cannot be or do without
Concept(Feel(), Lemma("feel"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), stimulus=Thing()))
Concept(See(), Lemma("see"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), stimulus=Thing()))
Concept(Hear(), Lemma("hear"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), stimulus=Thing()))
Concept(Mean(), Lemma("mean"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                       // words mean something
Concept(Choose(), Lemma("choose"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Thing(), source=Thing()))
Concept(Prefer(), Lemma("prefer"), Frame(experiencer=Someone(), theme=Thing(), standard=Thing()))
Concept(Try(), Lemma("try"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Act()))
Concept(Can(), Lemma("can"), Frame(agent=Thing(), theme=Act()))
Concept(Maybe(), Lemma("maybe"), Frame(Prop()))
Concept(Because(), Lemma("because"), Frame(Prop(), reason=Prop()))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Speech

Concept(Say(), Lemma("say"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Thing(), recipient=Someone()))
Concept(Answer(), Lemma("answer"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Thing(), topic=Thing()))  // say in reply to a question

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Events and doing

Concept(Do(), Lemma("do"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Act()))
Concept(Happen(), Lemma("happen"), Frame(theme=Thing()))
Concept(Cause(), Lemma("cause"), Frame(agent=Thing(), result=Prop()))
Concept(Become(), Lemma("become"), Frame(Prop()))                         // begin to hold
Concept(Begin(), Lemma("begin"), Lemma("start"), Frame(theme=Thing()))
Concept(End(), Lemma("end"), Frame(theme=Thing()))                        // stop happening or holding
Concept(Continue(), Lemma("continue"), Frame(theme=Thing()))              // go on happening or holding
Concept(Again(), Lemma("again"), Frame(Prop()))                           // one more time, after before
Concept(Change(), Lemma("change"), Frame(theme=Thing(), result=Prop()))   // become other than it was
Concept(Make(), Lemma("make"), Frame(agent=Someone(), product=Thing(), material=Thing()))
Concept(Move(), Lemma("move"), Frame(agent=Thing(), theme=Thing(), source=Place(), destination=Place()))
Concept(Use(), Lemma("use"), Frame(agent=Someone(), theme=Thing(), purpose=Act()))
Concept(Wait(), Lemma("wait"), Frame(agent=Someone(), time=Time()))       // do nothing until
Concept(Live(), Lemma("live"), Frame(Thing()))                            // is alive, is running

// How "cause" and "make" take what they bring about (stage 0, seed/CHANGES.md). Definitions are
// written in these two constructions more than in any other ("cause to remember", "make
// visible"), and no import gives them: VerbNet has no "NP V NP to VP" frame for "cause" and no
// "NP V NP ADJP" frame for "make". Without them no definition built on them is heard whole.
Fact(Cause(), Category(Act(), Takes(side=Right(), category=Thing(), role=Patient()), Takes(side=Right(), category=Act(), role=Result(), head=To())))
Reading(on=Cause(), pattern=Cause(patient=$p, result=$a), becomes=Cause(result=WithRoles($a, agent=$p)))
Fact(Make(), Category(Act(), Takes(side=Right(), category=Thing(), role=Patient()), Takes(side=Right(), category=Property(), role=Result())))
Reading(on=Make(), pattern=Make(patient=$p, result=$v), becomes=Cause(result=Become(Be($p, $v))))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Time (beyond the structural time heads Now, Past, Future, At, Since, Until, During, Before,
// After, Told, LastChange)

Concept(Moment(), Lemma("moment"), Lemma("time"), IsA(Time()))           // a point in time ("what time is it")
Concept(Duration(), Lemma("for some time"), Frame(Thing()))               // how long it holds

// What times are counted in, on the clock and the calendar. Lasts(n) is a unit's length in
// seconds (structural: Schedule reads it to work out "in 10 minutes"). Now() gives the present
// moment with these as its roles (year=, month=, day=, weekday=, hour=, minute=), so what is said
// about a time is said from them. Weekday(n) is a day's place in the week, Monday first (ISO 8601).
Concept(Minute(), Lemma("minute"), IsA(Duration()), Lasts(60))
Concept(Hour(), Lemma("hour"), IsA(Duration()), Lasts(3600))
Concept(Day(), Lemma("day"), Lemma("date"), IsA(Time()), IsA(Duration()), Lasts(86400))  // a date is a day, as the calendar names it
Concept(Week(), Lemma("week"), IsA(Duration()), Lasts(604800))
Concept(Month(), Lemma("month"), IsA(Time()))
Concept(Year(), Lemma("year"), IsA(Time()))
Concept(Weekday(), Frame(Number()))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Space

Concept(Here(), Lemma("here"), IsA(Place()))
Concept(Near(), Lemma("near"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))
Concept(Far(), Lemma("far"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))
Concept(Above(), Lemma("above"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))
Concept(Below(), Lemma("below"), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))
Concept(Side(), Lemma("side"), Frame(Thing()))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Documents (design section 25b). Hearing produces these from marks; Speaking's output is made of
// them, and the media realizations print them.

Concept(Document(), Lemma("document"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Text(), Lemma("text"), Frame(Thing()))                            // a run of words, as content
Concept(Paragraph(), Lemma("paragraph"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Heading(), Lemma("heading"), Frame(Thing(), level=Number()))
Concept(List(), Lemma("list"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Item(), Lemma("item"), Frame(Thing()))
Concept(Task(), Lemma("task"), Frame(Thing(), done=Prop()))
Concept(Contrast(), Lemma("contrast"), Frame(Thing()))                    // this, as against the alternatives
Concept(Withdrawn(), Frame(Thing()))                                      // said, then taken back
Concept(Inserted(), Frame(Thing()))                                       // the added side of a correction
Concept(Callout(), Frame(Thing(), kind=Kind()))                           // the writer's own words, flagged
Concept(Code(), Lemma("code"), Frame(Thing()))                            // a name or text to be taken exactly
Concept(CodeBlock(), Frame(Thing(), language=Kind()))
Concept(Link(), Lemma("link"), Frame(Thing(), to=Thing()))
Concept(Image(), Lemma("image"), Frame(Thing(), alt=Thing()))
Concept(Note(), Lemma("note"), Frame(Thing()))                            // a footnote: belongs where it is cited
Concept(LineBreak(), Lemma("line break"))
Concept(Tip(), Lemma("tip"), IsA(Kind()))                                 // a callout kind
Concept(Warning(), Lemma("warning"), IsA(Kind()))                         // a callout kind
Concept(Caution(), Lemma("caution"), IsA(Kind()))                         // a callout kind

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What the assistant learns to use (design section 25): the kinds every tool, service and source
// it learns is filed under. They pass the test of built-ins.md section 1: a chess assistant learns
// an engine's commands and options, a jam website's assistant a shop's API and its operations,
// and both look things up somewhere; none of these kinds is any one tool's, service's or
// source's. What belongs to what is PartOf (a command PartOf its tool, an option PartOf its
// command, an operation PartOf its API, a parameter PartOf its operation); a service spoken to
// through a program is ServedBy it. Command and Option are also the names of a usage line's parts
// (Read of a manual page): the same things, written down. Source is the role (where something
// starts), so where knowledge comes from is KnowledgeSource, said "source".

Concept(Tool(), Lemma("tool"), IsA(Program()))                            // a program on this machine, run by its name
Concept(Command(), Lemma("command"), IsA(Program()))                      // what a tool does when told
Concept(Option(), Lemma("option"))                                        // what changes how a command does it
Concept(Api(), Lemma("api"))                                              // a service spoken to over HTTP
Concept(Operation(), Lemma("operation"))                                  // what a service does when asked
Concept(Parameter(), Lemma("parameter"))                                  // what an operation is told
Concept(KnowledgeSource(), Lemma("source"))                               // where what is known comes from
Concept(ServedBy(), Frame(Thing(), Thing()))                              // reached through another: an API through its program

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The assistant itself: what it holds about the one addressed in every conversation, so a
// question about it is answered from here (design section 14b), never from the world's sources.

Fact(Addressee(), Name("Noodle"))
Fact(Addressee(), State(Good()))
